# G8 acceptance gates — closeout regression (2026-09-14)

## Schema-drift cleanup (the opportunistic batch)

Columns added idempotently via nocobase-crm-modules.mts (double-run kept):

- crm_products: active (bool, backfill true) / unit_price (backfill base_price)
  / sku (backfill SKU-CRM-####)
- crm_quotes: quote_number (backfill quote_no) / revision_note / createdAt
  (backfill issue_date)
- crm/global-search.tsx: dropped filters the seeded tables never had —
  customers phone (→ name), leads email (removed), deals title (→ name);
  DealRecord type carries both title and name (hub vs crm sources).

Effect: the e2e filters this batch touched no longer raise column errors,
but the claim that the full run's PG tail had zero `column … does not
exist` overstated it — the crm_leads.email family (and, seen live on
2026-09-14, crm_deals.contact_id on the contact-show deals rollup) still
throws; those residuals are registered for the H-round cleanup. Baseline
moves 58/23 → **59 passed / 22 failed**; the remaining 22 are pre-existing
data-semantics/UI-shape assertions (leads conversion-rate non-zero,
saved-view menu shape, customer-detail timeline, login-session reload,
drawer-select, bulk actions…), recorded per the batch instruction as out of
scope for column backfills. auth.setup.ts follows the G6 landing change
(/overview + English "Overview" heading).

